Audio + shared helper: an apps-SMMU stage-1 context of our own (new bsd/dev/negroni_smmu_s1.c) for the ADSP
stream 0x1801: the speaker ring anywhere in RAM, mapped at IOVA 0x10000000 (Android qcom,msm-audio-ion pool), given
to the ADSP as IOVA | 1 << 32 (msm_audio_ion.c SID bits). 0243 asked for a ring below 4 GiB: impossible, XNU RAM
starts at 0x840000000. Default OFF since 2026-10-27: negroniaudio_smmu=1 opts in; the default 0 keeps the old
physical path (fails cleanly: ring not below 4 GiB). Camera (0317, negronicam_smmu=3) uses the helper too.
2026-10-27 rework after the first boot with it panicked (Kernel data abort ESR 0x96000010 at the CBAR(74) restore
in undo(): Gunyah refused writing the old CBAR, type S2_TRANS): every setup/teardown access through
negroni_mmio_try_rd32/wr32 (0297; a refusal is an error, no panic; no stage-1 context without that hook);
teardown as Linux arm_smmu_destroy_domain_context: SCTLR 0 + TLB invalidate, CBAR/CBA2R never written back
(bank kept as "released", reused by us); banks from the bottom up from IDR1.NUMS2CB (Linux), U-Boot CBAR rule +
SCTLR.M 0 + no S2CR into it + TLBSTATUS idle, the claim write (CBA2R 1, CBAR 0x1f300, read back) is the test, a
refused bank is skipped (8 tries); TLB sync up to 500 ms (Linux TLB_LOOP_TIMEOUT; was 10 ms) with TBU/TCU ack
diagnostics on a time-out. New: negronismmu_probe=1|2 (default 0) surveys every bank at boot (reads + same-value
CBAR write, 1 = dormant banks only, 2 = all) into negroni_smmu_cb_verdict[]; the text again in the log after
negronismmu_probe_again s (default 60) and in sysctl kern.negroni_smmu_probe (root). Review fixes: report/fsr and the
ON lines through the refusable accessors, SCTLR written only after the claim and only when not 0, probe-REFUSED/
CHANGED banks skipped. SMRs still from the top down;
claim lock negroni_smmu_claim_lock for every SMMU user (Wi-Fi 0325 to take it). Details: patches/xnu/README-camera.md
"0317-0318, 0249" (2026-10-27 rework), docs/notes.md section 45.
